      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "A positive integer has an odd number of divisors exactly when it is a perfect square. The squares below \\(50\\) are \\[ 1,4,9,16,25,36,49, \\] so there are \\(7.\\)\n\nThus the correct answer is C.",
